    "https://hr.gatech.edu/employment/hr.gatech.edu/2026/01/07/career-boosters-georgia-techs-new-learning-program-empowers-professionals-to-grow/": {
      "title": "Career Boosters: Georgia Tech’s New Learning Program Empowers Professionals to Grow",
      "description": "Career Boosters: Georgia Tech’s New Learning Program Empowers Professionals to Grow  – Human Resources Skip to content Human Resources Careers About Who is HR? Our Strategic Plan News Events Working at Tech Employee Homepage Learning & Development Telework Agreements Employee Relations Global Human Resources Payroll Time & Labor Compensation & Classification Student Employment Leading at Tech People Leaders Performance Management Organizational Design & Effectiveness Change Management Benefits Engagement Learning & Development Forms & Guides Search Toggle search interface Menu Toggle extended navigation Career Boosters: Georgia Tech’s New Learning Program Empowers Professionals to Grow Publication date January 7, 2026 Categories: News Career Boosters Empowers Professionals to Grow In the ever-evolving landscape of professional development, standing still is not an option. At Georgia Tech, the message is clear: Growth is a journey, and the new Career Boosters resources are here to assist you. Career Boosters is a suite of resources designed to help Georgia Tech community members take meaningful steps forward as they navigate their careers. Whether you’re looking to sharpen your skills, expand your network, or gain clarity on your next move, Career Boosters can help with various areas of focus. Mentoring: Professional Partnerships Experience is a powerful catalyst for growth. Career Boosters leverages this by intentionally connecting participants with colleagues who serve as thought partners. Through these mentoring partnerships, one can gain practical insights into leadership, navigating organizational dynamics, and making informed career decisions. More than advice, these relationships foster mutual learning, strengthen professional networks, and contribute to a more connected and collaborative Georgia Tech community. Shadowing and Coaching: Learn From the Best Shadowing gives you the chance to find out what your dream role could look like. It offers a front-row seat to the responsibilities, challenges, and rhythms of roles you aspire to. It’s a powerful way to test the waters before diving in. But sometimes shadowing isn’t enough, and what you need most is a personal guide who can help you navigate your unique path. Career Boosters offers coaching sessions tailored to individual goals. These sessions help participants identify strengths, overcome obstacles, and chart a clear course forward. Professional Branding: Communicate Your Value In today’s digital-first world, how you present yourself matters. The curated learning path helps participants build skills to refine their professional brand. Whether it’s polishing your resume or mastering the art of the elevator pitch, this curated learning path ensures you’re seen and remembered for the right reasons. Click here to explore Career Boosters and sign up for the opportunities that best fit your professional goals. Related Post navigation Culture Champions Nominations Now Open Winter Storm Modified Operations, Inclement Weather Time Reporting Details Georgia Institute of Technology North Avenue Atlanta, GA 30332 Related +1 404.894.2000 Campus Map General Directory Employment Emergency Information Legal Legal & Privacy Information Human Trafficking Notice Title IX/Sexual Misconduct Hazing Public Disclosures Accessibility Accountability Accreditation Equal Opportunity, Nondiscrimination, and Anti-Harassment Policy Report Free Speech and Censorship Concerns © 2026 Georgia Institute of Technology close menu Careers About Toggle \"About\" submenu Who is HR? Our Strategic Plan News Events Working at Tech Toggle \"Working at Tech\" submenu Employee Homepage Learning & Development Telework Agreements Employee Relations Global Human Resources Payroll Time & Labor Compensation & Classification Student Employment Leading at Tech Toggle \"Leading at Tech\" submenu People Leaders Performance Management Organizational Design & Effectiveness Change Management Benefits Engagement Learning & Development close search Search Search Site This website uses cookies. For more information, review our Privacy & Legal Notice . \r\n    Questions? Please email privacy@gatech.edu . x"
    },
